Apple-provided dynamic libraries
--------------------------------
The runtime executable and libpython3.14.dylib dynamically link these macOS
libraries:

- /usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib
- /usr/lib/libz.1.dylib
- /usr/lib/libedit.3.dylib
- /usr/lib/libncurses.5.4.dylib
- /usr/lib/libpanel.5.4.dylib
- CoreFoundation.framework
- SystemConfiguration.framework

These libraries are provided by macOS and are not included in Goblin. Their
licenses are not redistributed. The readline module is a built-in module whose
backend is editline. The build's -lreadline flag resolves to the system libedit,
so Goblin does not contain GNU Readline or its GPL license text.

Pruned components
-----------------
The release build removes these from the app bundle. They are present in the
upstream archive and the development cache but are not redistributed:

- pip 26.2.1 and ensurepip
- idle, idlelib and the idle3 command wrappers
- the pydoc command wrappers
- tkinter and _tkinter
- Tcl/Tk 9.0.4 (Tcl 9.0.4 and Tk 9.0.4), Itcl 4.3.8, Thread 3.0.6 and their
  dylibs and data
- test, turtledemo, config, pkgconfig, include and share

No license text for these components is included in the app bundle.

